Cell[TextData[{
 "A vertex list is an open walk. A cycle graph is a closed walk, read \
cyclically. A list of walk graphs gives ",
 Cell[BoxData["True"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ca514396-a794-4afc-815f-7bf0fac826b4"],
 " when every one is generic."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"83d1c5b5-9c57-4b3d-bdee-83defe663a6c"],

Cell["\<\
On a graph two strands that cross at a vertex must leave it along different \
edges. On the square grid that forces one strand horizontal and the other \
vertical at the crossing; a crossing snapped from a diagonal usually shares \
an edge, a self-tangency.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9cd0be5b-89d4-48d2-a23d-9de7ea9ca632"]
}, Open  ]],

